<title>BELGIUM: RESEARCH ALERT - Ackermans downgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Ackermans downgraded.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of research report -</p>
<p>Co name-----------Sector------Price------Broker-------------</p>
<p>    Ackermans vH	Holding     8,070  *   Vermeulen Raendonck</p>
<p>COMMENT: shares of holding company Ackermans &amp; Van Haaren NV (AVH) have risen 59 percent since Vermeulen's 'buy' recommendation on October 29, compared to 30 percent for the Bel-20. It estimates the net asset value of the share at 8,153 francs. AVH's current discount to NAV is thus only one percent. The brokerage said that AVH's discount should range between zero and 10 percent, compared to 10 to 25 percent for other holding companies and downgraded AVH to 'hold' from 'buy'.</p>
<p>Analyst: Francois Poullet, tel 32 2 547 38 96</p>
<p>(*) Date of research report: June 20, 1997  Estimates:   EPS	  pvs est   P/E</p>
<p> 1997	   343 BFR    (n/a)     23.5</p>
<p> 1998	   390 BFR</p>
